// Human labels for judge calibration. One JSON object per line:
//   {"example_id": "open-001", "label": "A" | "B" | "tie", "annotator": "you"}
//
// "A" means the CANDIDATE response was better, "B" the baseline, "tie" neither.
// Labels are only meaningful against the exact pair of responses the annotator
// saw, so regenerate the sheet whenever the arms change:
//
//   python scripts/eval.py --candidate assistant@v2 --baseline assistant@v1 --json
//
// Target ~100 labelled comparisons. Below that the agreement interval is wider
// than the differences it is being used to judge.
//
// This file is intentionally empty. Fabricated labels would produce a kappa that
// measures nothing while looking like calibration, which is worse than none.
